From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: edwardzhu02 <explodingtnt@foxmail.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 23:06:25 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] OSLoader: NAND dump and restore firmwares over USB CDC

Two RAM-loaded variants that run on the 39gII without touching the
installed system:

- DUMP_ONLY (nandump.c): stream every page (data + 19 B metadata) to the
  host.
- RESTORE_ONLY (nandrestore.c, new): write pages back, erase blocks, read
  pages and verify pages against host-supplied data.

Both use TinyUSB CDC.  The CDC RX buffer was only 512 B at high speed,
which silently dropped bytes in 2 KB frames, so raise RX to 4 KB and TX
to 2 KB.

Lessons baked into the restore path:
- host must pace frames (256 B every 3 ms); faster bursts overflow.
- the buffer handed to the GPMI write DMA must be 32-byte aligned and
  separate from the CDC receive buffer, otherwise non-uniform pages
  silently fail to program while uniform fills appear to work.
- the task re-arms per connection (banner + RX flush) instead of serving
  one session and parking.

Verified on hardware: full dump 65536/65536 pages with 0 bad frames;
full restore 10377 pages written, 55159 blank pages skipped, 0
failures; a subsequent full dump is byte-identical in both data and OOB.
